{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0810525c4f98fb835b0c70c6eb56e5b0738a42da9913e318c79bbca598ac2b77","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_10acc7e1920384215422d497964100c9a10bd24c3074acc62361be0c3b1ad42e"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"The --delegate flag injects a scoped MCP belt exposing only ask/plan/run/best-of/status/result tools, with nesting depth 1, a default cap of 8 sub-runs per parent, and shared daemon-owned budget authority; only adapters declaring mcp_injection (claude, codex, cursor) can host it.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2fa9ca3b579f0d06808d44370250f41ebb4d5cf4da73009235b38eba9b13bcf6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_79fb93eeeef229e9b6e837ef3a0eca6955118deffff283f42cf16b3916f50be4"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"Canonical modes are ask (read-only, with --deep-scan multi-scout research), plan (with --council parallel multi-harness drafting merged into one plan), and agent (with --n best-of races, --attempts repair loops, --until-clean, and --delegate).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_402693a36a8723f2b7ebcf0ceaf4da9991dd76d46155796b5afd94b555987739","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c25fba4dc9f676d9b6f58df6d771824e7693cf7394f5e317079eb081b8d668a6","slc_c406422b854dd3ab45c5e764a47d956a397d108e22baf106c26135b9e9f7e72a"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"Live subscription-quota tracking and auto-rotation on typed vendor limits cover only harnesses with a vendor usage source (Antigravity, Claude, Codex); Cursor has none yet, and the portable Copilot plugin does not support Windows.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_82d8c8082968192cff8bc2d1973c3f0392484bf2d0594c05a0978fc069470640","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c25fba4dc9f676d9b6f58df6d771824e7693cf7394f5e317079eb081b8d668a6"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"The product is local-first: everything runs on the user's machine, files are the source of truth, and the README states there is no telemetry.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_85b684cefe7b1f6b226965d2a9dd5af31985b68cc7d2b0eb6aa4b2f500aa84e7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_03da5186cbb9fa92532f263453f469063cb5fe64210bbf9df1ac320cccce0e71","slc_c81d64b0a0e1fc345fe51aa289614f64d43a9feec50af622153684fc44e58b7d"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"Read-only ask/plan turns resume the routed harness's native CLI session in a durable per-lane home; lane switches hydrate with a bounded continuation packet written to context/THREAD.md and disclosed via a typed session.continuity event.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a39f962ad548fdcf53b8eef7ca576ca0ca85389d77dcefe5153c2ce3948092be","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4b9056ac6c6c5224ffabe166bf52cd5cd7aa38212418e5d518f1d134b76ba3d5","slc_ae2aad1ea2cf777a8b09a707a45872c5d4e95de1e869fc2dfefc058da4287882","slc_ce700b99f2a0bcb0c5f5bab9ef3d942bbd49d2e46b91737b417be46e51d66852"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"Retired mode ids and verbs (audit, best_of_n, explore, orchestrate, etc.) hard-error with the new spelling rather than silently aliasing; unknown flags and invalid flag values exit with code 2.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ad2dff2d84b335eb4f7eff67ce8f546c835e0d16c5f42cc29097890abd4f63be","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_730185287ac32e38d8c2fba0a2ed3fcd77fb5670c93b397119474637ec390139"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors build with pnpm install --frozen-lockfile and pnpm build, then run typecheck, test, schema:gen with a generated-diff check, docs:check, and knip as gates.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_af2858ff9d218bc0cd948fea8072c18afb3e3502a408f43058d8204a7413a725","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_07f8c4c886a780474b2dcd5e7bbb83161d63380448fa3a22cf52dab5ed0644b9","slc_6b452ac7c99a3707d0e72acf75aed48ddd8d9e2f828bf907db5a8250672d50d9","slc_935cc786b5712660f3d98bf8cddfc1c8ea17b8b3c0dc25efde9a5d22e8eefe73"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"Claudexor exposes a CLI, a loopback HTTP/SSE control API scoped to /v2 with POST /v2/handshake negotiation, MCP, ACP, and a macOS app as thin surfaces over the daemon.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bb1ab7016a50d34c290b9ae46b34ea7ccd6e138e086fa52fce55a6e40a231f89","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2db2590c43bf118c5aba15c7f33453904da3035a1185977330302141eaf785d4","slc_c011066b094d4be21d58b6a4b3b1cea32cabcce6cc140ca4dcc0de81157ce48d"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"Protected paths configured in .claudexor/config.yaml pause apply for a human decision; --allow-protected-path covers only engine-derived gate/test paths and cannot suppress project rules, and mutating turns on such projects are promoted one-way to an isolated worktree.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c1ef2f2c1496e9431403bbc215544bd8b2183f9bfa98dde0acf90dce1378fb55","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8cb4dafe7b4221e0d8f03be391872587cfb3fc19682ed5805c4ff591d4fdf5ab"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"Prerequisites are Node.js >= 20.19, pnpm via corepack, Git for Git-backed worktrees, and at least one logged-in vendor CLI (codex, claude, cursor-agent, opencode, or agy) or a provider API key; the desktop app requires macOS while the CLI/daemon also run on Linux.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d85b7930f41e70ca2aded742293af598331bce9a603873cfbcfca875f9e16088","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a7b1a3353f98d375efe36b375617a7d4997d0e10fa1dfe905f0ef46a8b65bba"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"Cost accounting is typed: paid budgets are explicit via --max-usd with zero as a real cap, unknown cost is never reported as $0, and runs can end cost_unverifiable or budget_overshoot.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e570d7b17b9d88894d3230dfc67c4d1fced1e9aded22b638681a1b3a508d9363","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"razzant/claudexor@87f08d28cf33 snapshot ffa685ceb1e6d91a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6b452ac7c99a3707d0e72acf75aed48ddd8d9e2f828bf907db5a8250672d50d9"],"source_ids":["src_8fb9d84d31015275b76d61e5f74a1070"],"text":"The monorepo splits packages/schema (contracts and generated JSON Schema), harness-* adapters, workspace (Git/directory envelopes), orchestrator (canonical mode pipelines), and review/arbitration/synthesis/budget packages.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7a1cf05348c7435f88daa1b2cb4b0186"}
